q:
A quadrilateral $ABCD$ satisfies $\angle A=\angle B=90^\circ$, $\angle C=45^\circ$, $AC=19$, and $BD=15$. Find its area. Here $XY$ denotes the length of segment $XY$.

[asy]
import geometry;
settings.tex="none";
defaultpen(black+linewidth(0.65));
size(310);
pair A=(0,1),B=(0,0),C=(3.2,0),D=(2.2,1);
draw(A--B--C--D--cycle);draw(A--C);draw(B--D);
label("A",A,(-1,1));label("B",B,(-1,-1));label("C",C,(1,-1));label("D",D,(1,1));
label("15",(0.65,0.43),(0,1));label("19",(2,0.45),(0,1));
[/asy]

Eleven Othello pieces are arranged in a row as in (a). Repeat the following flipping operation:

Choose two nonadjacent pieces whose face-up colors are the same and such that all pieces between them have the other color. Flip all the pieces between them simultaneously.

How many sequences of flips lead to the arrangement in (b)? Each piece has one black face and one white face.

[asy]
import geometry;
settings.tex="none";
defaultpen(black+linewidth(0.65));
size(640);
for(int p=0;p<2;++p){real shift=p*14.5;label(p==0?"(a)":"(b)",(shift-0.9,0));for(int k=0;k<11;++k)filldraw(circle((shift+k,0),0.38),p==1||k%2==0?black:white,black+linewidth(0.65));}
[/asy]
